cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "MicroHTGR: A Modular OpenMC Neutronics and Depletion Framework for Prismatic High-Temperature Gas-Cooled Reactors"
abstract: >-
  A configuration-driven OpenMC framework for full-core neutronics, criticality
  search, spatially resolved depletion, and coupled neutronics/thermal-hydraulics
  analysis of prismatic high-temperature gas-cooled reactors. Core layout, fuel,
  reactivity control, reflectors and depletion schedules are all defined in a
  single parameter file, so a wide range of prismatic HTGR cores can be analysed
  without modifying the source. Developed for, and demonstrated on, the Compact
  Helium-cooled Universal Defense Reactor (CHUDR) senior design project.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Finney
    given-names: Cade
    email: finney.cade@ufl.edu
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Materials Science and Engineering, Nuclear Engineering
      Program, University of Florida
repository-code: "https://github.com/c-finney/MicroHTGR"
